Upstream sources and their terms
--------------------------------
bio.tools — the ELIXIR registry of life-science software.
    https://bio.tools · content under CC BY 4.0.
    Assayer selects records from 12 drug-discovery EDAM topics; the records
    are theirs, the selection and the staging are ours. This dataset is
    licensed CC BY 4.0 in turn, as that licence requires.

GitHub repository metadata — names, URLs, descriptions, stars, licences and
    push dates, retrieved through the public API. Facts about public
    repositories; each repository remains under its own licence.

PyPI and conda-forge package metadata — retrieved through their public APIs.

Curated entries, stage taxonomy, protocols, gates and usage examples are
    original work by the Assayer authors, released here under CC BY 4.0.

Structure data (UniProt, RCSB PDB, AlphaFold DB) is fetched live by the
    browser at use time and is not redistributed in this repository.
